## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses hands-on planning expertise across REST and WebSocket streaming, tenant isolation, contracts, and resilience—areas often under-tested in real-time systems but critical for production reliability.

## Key Concepts

- **Contract Testing**: Validate agreements between gateway and downstream services using PACT or similar frameworks to ensure API compatibility.
- **WebSocket Streaming**: Test connectivity, message ordering, heartbeats, and backpressure handling under load.
- **Per-Tenant Isolation**: Verify data separation through keys, partitions, and role-based access controls to prevent cross-tenant leakage.
- **Fault Injection**: Test circuit breakers, retry logic, and fallback mechanisms when downstream services throttle or fail.
- **Observability**: Implement OpenTelemetry traces, structured logs, and dashboards for visibility into system behavior.
- **End-to-End SLAs**: Validate latency, throughput, and data integrity requirements per tenant.

## Code Example

```java
@Test
void shouldIsolateTenantsInWebSocketStream() {
    String tenantA = "tenant-a-key";
    String tenantB = "tenant-b-key";

    WebSocketClient clientA = new WebSocketClient(wsUrl, tenantA);
    WebSocketClient clientB = new WebSocketClient(wsUrl, tenantB);

    clientA.connect();
    clientB.connect();

    clientA.send("telemetry:update", payloadA);
    clientB.send("telemetry:update", payloadB);

    assertThat(clientA.receive()).doesNotContain(payloadB);
    assertThat(clientB.receive()).doesNotContain(payloadA);
}
```

## Test Cases

| Category | Test Case | Acceptance Criteria |
|----------|-----------|---------------------|
| REST | Concurrent tenant requests | Each tenant receives only their own data |
| WebSocket | Backpressure under high message rate | Messages queue without dropping or timing out |
| Contract | Gateway matches downstream schema | PACT verification passes |
| Resilience | Downstream timeout | Gateway returns 503 within SLA |
| Throttling | Rate limit exceeded | 429 with proper retry-after header |

## Why This Is Asked

This question validates a candidate's ability to test file upload endpoints, covering authorization, input validation, error handling, and resilience patterns. Beginners should demonstrate familiarity with content-type validation, size limits, idempotency mechanisms, and rate limiting in a CI-friendly test suite.

## Key Concepts

- Multipart/form-data requests and file type validation (allowlists)
- Idempotency keys and Retry-After header semantics
- Per-user rate limiting and error code mapping (400, 401, 413, 415, 429)
- CI integration using tooling such as Postman/Newman or pytest

## Code Example

```javascript
// POST /api/v1/uploads test suite
describe('POST /api/v1/uploads', () => {
  it('returns 401 without Authorization header', async () => {
    const res = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/uploads')
      .attach('file', Buffer.from('test'), 'test.pdf');
    expect(res.status).toBe(401);
  });

  it('returns 415 for unsupported file types', async () => {
    const res = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/uploads')
      .set('Authorization', 'Bearer valid-token')
      .attach('file', Buffer.from('test'), 'test.exe');
    expect(res.status).toBe(415);
  });

  it('returns 413 when file exceeds 5MB', async () => {
    const largeFile = Buffer.alloc(6 * 1024 * 1024);
    const res = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/uploads')
      .set('Authorization', 'Bearer valid-token')
      .attach('file', largeFile, 'large.pdf');
    expect(res.status).toBe(413);
  });

  it('deduplicates requests with Idempotency-Key', async () => {
    const key = 'unique-key-123';
    const res1 = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/uploads')
      .set('Authorization', 'Bearer valid-token')
      .set('Idempotency-Key', key)
      .attach('file', Buffer.from('content'), 'doc.pdf');
    const res2 = await request(app)
      .post('/api/v1/uploads')
      .set('Authorization', 'Bearer valid-token')
      .set('Idempotency-Key', key)
      .attach('file', Buffer.from('content'), 'doc.pdf');
    expect(res1.body.uploadId).toBe(res2.body.uploadId);
  });

  it('returns 429 when rate limit exceeded', async () => {
    const requests = Array(3).fill(null).map(() =>
      request(app).post('/api/v1/uploads').set('Authorization', 'Bearer valid-token')
    );
    const results = await Promise.all(requests);
    expect(results.some(r => r.status === 429)).toBe(true);
  });
});
```

